    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/A99CE46A67143A8F77A8C7BDEA7155DA/jobs/565450": {
      "title": "Director of Neuropsychology Emphasis Area",
      "description": "Director of Neuropsychology Emphasis Area You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Neuropsychology Emphasis Area Spalding-Mansion - Louisville, KY 40203 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Doctorate/PhD Category Education Apply Description Director of Neuropsychology Emphasis Area The School of Professional Psychology (SOPP) at Spalding University is hiring for a Director of our Neuropsychology Emphasis Area within our doctoral program. Fully accredited since 1989, our doctoral program is highly successful, with a strong national reputation. JOB SUMMARY We are seeking candidates who will continue building upon our incredibly strong program, teaching and training in accordance with the Minnesota Conference Guidelines. Anyone hired would also be expected to achieve a strong balance across the three domains of teaching, scholarship, and service. First, they will be strong clinician-educators who utilize best practices in teaching and enjoy student mentoring. Ideally, they will also be competent in supervision and support neuropsychological training within our department training clinic, the Center for Behavioral Health. Second, they will be thoughtful scholars with either a record of presenting and/or publishing in their chosen research interest areas or demonstrated promise to do so. Third, they will possess strong interpersonal skills and a cooperative spirit to work collegially with others on university and departmental service committees. Candidates must hold a doctoral degree in clinical or counseling psychology, either with or immediate eligibility for licensure in KY as a psychologist. Excellent early career candidates will be considered, with mentorship and supervision provided if needed for licensure. The position offers scheduling flexibility (other than class times) and faculty members are encouraged to use up to eight hours per week in research, consultation, direct service (e.g. private practice) and/or supervision. Opportunities are available to engage in direct service as part of our Faculty Practice Plan, where faculty can see their own private practice clients in the Center for Behavioral Health. Additional contract supervision for doctoral students on practicum may also be available. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Teach six graduate courses in the School of Professional Psychology, including the four Neuropsychology Emphasis Area classes Develop or continue a scholarship interest area (and create opportunities to mentor students in their own scholarship) Contribute service to the department and university (e.g., active participation on committees) Mentor students’ dissertation research Assist with the development and maintenance of neuropsychology practicum sites Attend faculty and departmental meetings and events Assist with recruitment and retention of students Qualifications SKILLS, EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENTS Must hold a doctoral degree in clinical or counseling psychology from an APA accredited program Must be license eligible or hold a valid license as a psychologist in Kentucky with designation for supervision or working toward it (i.e., HSP designation) Teaching and supervision experience strongly preferred, but not required Established research interests strongly preferred, but not required Must have strong interpersonal skills Must have strong oral and written communication skills INTERRELATIONS Must have an appreciation and respect for the diverse, intersecting identities of students and colleagues Will have regular contact with administration, faculty, staff, and students Individual and group faculty mentoring available for the first year of employment CONTACT All applications are made through the Paycom Applicant Tracking System. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Norah Chapman, SOPP Associate Chair at nchapman02@spalding.edu ABOUT SPALDING UNIVERSITY: Spalding University offers a comprehensive package including medical, dental, vision, Spalding matching contribution up to 5% to your 403b/Roth retirement plan, generous Paid Time Off program, Parental Leave, paid holidays, paid life insurance and long-term disability, paid time for volunteering, and more. Situated in the heart of downtown Louisville, Kentucky’s largest city, Spalding University combines a rich social justice history and a commitment to community service as we attract students who desire a high-quality education in a very personalized setting. An engaged faculty serves nearly 2,000 students at the bachelors’, master’s and doctoral levels, providing real-world learning in liberal and professional studies. Faculty, staff and students are united by the institutional mission: Spalding University is a diverse community of learners dedicated to meeting the needs of the times in the tradition of the Sisters of Charity of Nazareth through quality undergraduate and graduate liberal and professional studies, grounded in spiritual values, with an emphasis on service and the promotion of peace and justice . With a focus on service and leadership, Spalding offers all students a mission-driven connection to community and comprehensive learning resources while striking a distinctive balance serving the educational needs of both the traditional student and the working student. In addition, our unique 8-week class delivery format affords students scheduling flexibility amidst other life responsibilities. Spalding aspires to become the first choice for students of compassion and service.  Celebrated for a rigorous yet nurturing environment, emulated for interdisciplinary collaborations, and acclaimed for contributions to the community. Spalding University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. The University complies with all federal, state and local equal employment opportunity laws. It is the University’s policy not to discriminate against any individual or group of individuals and to provide equal employment opportunity to all qualified persons regardless of race, color, national origin, age, disability, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, military status, veteran status or other protected status. All job offers are contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
